      "writtenOn": "2022-12-03T05:08:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The observation is correct. Is your concern that the client could be blocked indefinitely waiting for `onTransferReady`? I don\u0027t think that it will be actually waiting because going from \u0027TRANSFERRING\u0027 to \u0027DRAINING\u0027 is only possible by means of the \u0027drain\u0027 command sent from the client. I think that waiting for the callback and sending the command at the same time would indicate lack of coordination in the client implementation. Also, sending a command implies getting a reply, which always provides the new stream state, thus the client will explicitly know that the stream is not in the \u0027TRANSFERRING\u0027 state anymore.",
      "parentUuid": "a9eeac25_cd64cf22",
